<title>FRANCE: Thomson 96 net attrib profit 745 mln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Thomson 96 net attrib profit 745 mln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable profit		    745  vs  loss     791</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)		     2.80  vs	    2.60</p>
<p>    Operating				    2,069  vs	   1,960</p>
<p>    Exceptional losses			   824  vs	     753</p>
<p>    Financial loss				  27  vs  loss     135</p>
<p>    Turnover				    36,271  vs	  35,497</p>
<p>    Consolidated pre-tax profit	   1,303   vs  loss     437</p>
<p>    Net financial debt			  900   vs	   2,300</p>
<p>    Attributable shareholders funds    13,715   vs	  12,504</p>
<p>    Net assets per share			115   vs	     108</p>
<p>NOTE - Thomson-CSF gave its results in a statement. It said with an order book with more than 67 billion francs at the end of 1996, the company should see an increase in consolidated turnover compared to last year on a like-for-like basis. The consolidated net result will depend on the accounting treatment for a potential exceptional capital gain on the possible sale of SGS-Thomson shares. The pre-tax results reflect a 101 million franc impact from its Credit Lyonnais holding sold on December 23 and provisions for depreciation on the stake.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
